{"parentUuid":"02453802-6ddf-4325-a54e-0870ad357b98","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad57881598683395e","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf4J1SMN2tugSdurmYAWW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016GE7kveWRm5ZZfCezRNi73","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference.md","prompt":"What does skillOverrides accept as values? What do skillListingBudgetFraction and skillListingMaxDescChars do?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1831,"cache_read_input_tokens":33797,"output_tokens":263,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":38},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1831},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":8,"output_tokens":263,"cache_read_input_tokens":33797,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1831,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016GE7kveWRm5ZZfCezRNi73":{"url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference.md","prompt":"What does skillOverrides accept as values? What do skillListingBudgetFraction and skillListingMaxDescChars do?"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cf4J1RjeLvCm6wFKXQUG6","attributionAgent":"claude-code-guide","type":"assistant","uuid":"5879700f-f59c-47b3-98d8-b99d541a3030","timestamp":"2026-09-15T00:40:17.440Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"83c30d83-83e3-464a-b3bb-0a18b5ea54cb","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"5879700f-f59c-47b3-98d8-b99d541a3030","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58366d6f-ebc8-4b8f-aaec-39fa7dcbe44b","agentId":"ad57881598683395e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016GE7kveWRm5ZZfCezRNi73","type":"tool_result","content":"# Skill Settings Overview\n\nBased on the documentation excerpt, here's what these three settings do:\n\n## `skillOverrides`\n**Values accepted:** This setting accepts configuration to **hide or collapse a skill** without editing its SKILL.md file. The exact value format isn't detailed in this excerpt, but it allows per-skill visibility control.\n\n- **Topic:** Plugins and skills\n- **Scope:** Any file\n- **Purpose:** Override skill visibility from settings\n\n## `skillListingBudgetFraction`\n**What it does:** Reserves more or less context for the [skill listing](/docs/en/skills#skill-descriptions-are-cut-short)\n\n- **Topic:** Memory and context\n- **Scope:** Any file\n- **Purpose:** Control how much of your context window is allocated to displaying available skills\n\n## `skillListingMaxDescChars`\n**What it does:** Caps each skill's description length in the skill listing\n\n- **Topic:** Memory and context\n- **Scope:** Any file\n- **Purpose:** Limit individual skill descriptions when they're displayed, preventing overly long skill descriptions from consuming context\n\n---\n\n**Related context:** These two settings work together to manage how much space skills take up in your context window. When skill descriptions are cut short, both the budget fraction and max description character limits help optimize context usage, as noted in the [skill descriptions documentation](/docs/en/skills#skill-descriptions-are-cut-short)."}]},"uuid":"6fc1d8aa-9828-44be-b785-0a1f9c7a2404","timestamp":"2026-09-15T00:40:22.258Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":436394,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Skill Settings Overview\n\nBased on the documentation excerpt, here's what these three settings do:\n\n## `skillOverrides`\n**Values accepted:** This setting accepts configuration to **hide or collapse a skill** without editing its SKILL.md file. The exact value format isn't detailed in this excerpt, but it allows per-skill visibility control.\n\n- **Topic:** Plugins and skills\n- **Scope:** Any file\n- **Purpose:** Override skill visibility from settings\n\n## `skillListingBudgetFraction`\n**What it does:** Reserves more or less context for the [skill listing](/docs/en/skills#skill-descriptions-are-cut-short)\n\n- **Topic:** Memory and context\n- **Scope:** Any file\n- **Purpose:** Control how much of your context window is allocated to displaying available skills\n\n## `skillListingMaxDescChars`\n**What it does:** Caps each skill's description length in the skill listing\n\n- **Topic:** Memory and context\n- **Scope:** Any file\n- **Purpose:** Limit individual skill descriptions when they're displayed, preventing overly long skill descriptions from consuming context\n\n---\n\n**Related context:** These two settings work together to manage how much space skills take up in your context window. When skill descriptions are cut short, both the budget fraction and max description character limits help optimize context usage, as noted in the [skill descriptions documentation](/docs/en/skills#skill-descriptions-are-cut-short).","durationMs":4721,"url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5879700f-f59c-47b3-98d8-b99d541a3030","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"83c30d83-83e3-464a-b3bb-0a18b5ea54cb","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"02453802-6ddf-4325-a54e-0870ad357b98","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58366d6f-ebc8-4b8f-aaec-39fa7dcbe44b","agentId":"ad57881598683395e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0191uBczMDzk5jABX9sEa5MS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Skill Invocation Control: Key Differences\n\n## `disable-model-invocation`\n\nSet `disable-model-invocation: true` to **prevent Claude from automatically invoking the skill**. You can still invoke it manually with `/skill-name`.\n\n**Effect on context:**\n- The skill's **description is NOT in context** for Claude\n- The full skill content loads only when you manually invoke it\n- Claude won't see it as an available option\n\n**Use case:** Side-effect operations you want to control, like `/deploy`, `/commit`, or `/send-slack-message`\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: deploy\ndescription: Deploy the application to production\ndisable-model-invocation: true\n---\n```\n\n## `user-invocable: false`\n\nSet `user-invocable: false` to **prevent you from invoking the skill manually**. Only Claude can invoke it.\n\n**Effect on context:**\n- The skill's **description IS in context** for Claude\n- Claude can load it automatically when relevant\n- You cannot type `/skill-name` to invoke it\n\n**Use case:** Background knowledge or reference material that shouldn't be a user-facing command, like a `legacy-system-context` skill\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: legacy-system-context\ndescription: How the old payment system works\nuser-invocable: false\n---\n```\n\n## Side-by-Side Comparison\n\n| Aspect | Default | `disable-model-invocation: true` | `user-invocable: false` |\n|--------|---------|----------------------------------|------------------------|\n| You can invoke | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ❌ No |\n| Claude can invoke | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |\n| Description in context | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |\n| When loaded | On invocation | On your invocation only | On Claude's invocation |\n\n## Skill Listing Visibility\n\nAccording to the documentation:\n\n> The `/skills` menu lists all skills. A skill with `disable-model-invocation: true` **removes the description from Claude's context** but keeps it visible in listings. The skill **remains in the `/skills` menu** since you can still manually invoke it.\n\nA skill with `user-invocable: false` also appears in the `/skills` menu but you won't be able to select it to invoke."}]},"uuid":"927232d6-87c3-4a31-a6ae-bdd79c49c9ec","timestamp":"2026-09-15T00:40:23.561Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":112699,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Skill Invocation Control: Key Differences\n\n## `disable-model-invocation`\n\nSet `disable-model-invocation: true` to **prevent Claude from automatically invoking the skill**. You can still invoke it manually with `/skill-name`.\n\n**Effect on context:**\n- The skill's **description is NOT in context** for Claude\n- The full skill content loads only when you manually invoke it\n- Claude won't see it as an available option\n\n**Use case:** Side-effect operations you want to control, like `/deploy`, `/commit`, or `/send-slack-message`\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: deploy\ndescription: Deploy the application to production\ndisable-model-invocation: true\n---\n```\n\n## `user-invocable: false`\n\nSet `user-invocable: false` to **prevent you from invoking the skill manually**. Only Claude can invoke it.\n\n**Effect on context:**\n- The skill's **description IS in context** for Claude\n- Claude can load it automatically when relevant\n- You cannot type `/skill-name` to invoke it\n\n**Use case:** Background knowledge or reference material that shouldn't be a user-facing command, like a `legacy-system-context` skill\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: legacy-system-context\ndescription: How the old payment system works\nuser-invocable: false\n---\n```\n\n## Side-by-Side Comparison\n\n| Aspect | Default | `disable-model-invocation: true` | `user-invocable: false` |\n|--------|---------|----------------------------------|------------------------|\n| You can invoke | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ❌ No |\n| Claude can invoke | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |\n| Description in context | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |\n| When loaded | On invocation | On your invocation only | On Claude's invocation |\n\n## Skill Listing Visibility\n\nAccording to the documentation:\n\n> The `/skills` menu lists all skills. A skill with `disable-model-invocation: true` **removes the description from Claude's context** but keeps it visible in listings. The skill **remains in the `/skills` menu** since you can still manually invoke it.\n\nA skill with `user-invocable: false` also appears in the `/skills` menu but you won't be able to select it to invoke.","durationMs":7009,"url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"02453802-6ddf-4325-a54e-0870ad357b98","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"83c30d83-83e3-464a-b3bb-0a18b5ea54cb","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
