{"parentUuid":"e9b3477b-8272-43ce-b84f-86123e2b644f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad57881598683395e","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf4J3ET3xhGWnuZwQHBtz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QLay6AwfXY4CDWqo8rfP3H","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills.md","prompt":"skill-descriptions-are-cut-short - what happens when skillListingBudgetFraction is exceeded? Are descriptions truncated? Are skill names shown without descriptions?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":521,"cache_read_input_tokens":37365,"output_tokens":176,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":54},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":521},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":8,"output_tokens":176,"cache_read_input_tokens":37365,"cache_creation_input_tokens":521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":521,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QLay6AwfXY4CDWqo8rfP3H":{"url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills.md","prompt":"skill-descriptions-are-cut-short - what happens when skillListingBudgetFraction is exceeded? Are descriptions truncated? Are skill names shown without descriptions?"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cf4J3DhQLxoqcncnKfKor","attributionAgent":"claude-code-guide","type":"assistant","uuid":"6a4d4be6-e409-4a36-9191-dd8d5e729ed4","timestamp":"2026-09-15T00:40:40.746Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"83c30d83-83e3-464a-b3bb-0a18b5ea54cb","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"6a4d4be6-e409-4a36-9191-dd8d5e729ed4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58366d6f-ebc8-4b8f-aaec-39fa7dcbe44b","agentId":"ad57881598683395e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QLay6AwfXY4CDWqo8rfP3H","type":"tool_result","content":"# Skill Descriptions Are Cut Short\n\nYes, skill descriptions are truncated when they exceed the context budget. According to the documentation:\n\n> Put the key use case first: the combined `description` and `when_to_use` text is truncated at 1,536 characters in the skill listing to reduce context usage.\n\n## How It Works\n\nWhen you define a skill's frontmatter, Claude Code combines the `description` and `when_to_use` fields:\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: my-skill\ndescription: What this skill does\nwhen_to_use: Additional context for when Claude should invoke the skill\n---\n```\n\nThe combined text is capped at **1,536 characters** in the skill listing shown to Claude. This truncation serves two purposes:\n\n1. **Reduces context usage**: Skill descriptions stay in context across every turn, so shorter descriptions mean lower token costs\n2. **Prioritizes key information**: You should put the most important use case first in the `description` field\n\n## Best Practices\n\nTo make the most of the 1,536-character budget:\n\n- **Lead with the key use case** in `description`\n- **Keep descriptions concise** — state the purpose clearly without unnecessary elaboration\n- **Use `when_to_use` for additional context** if needed, but recognize it shares the same budget\n- **Write your full detailed instructions in the skill body** (`SKILL.md` content), which loads only when invoked\n\nFor example:\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: commit\ndescription: Stage and commit changes to git\nwhen_to_use: Use when you want to save your work with a descriptive message\n---\n\n1. Stage files with git add\n2. Create a commit with a clear message\n...\n```\n\nThe full skill content only loads when the skill is actually invoked, so verbose instructions don't cost tokens until needed."}]},"uuid":"21cbe1f4-5c7c-4e23-8775-e7aa7f6bf143","timestamp":"2026-09-15T00:40:46.844Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":112699,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Skill Descriptions Are Cut Short\n\nYes, skill descriptions are truncated when they exceed the context budget. According to the documentation:\n\n> Put the key use case first: the combined `description` and `when_to_use` text is truncated at 1,536 characters in the skill listing to reduce context usage.\n\n## How It Works\n\nWhen you define a skill's frontmatter, Claude Code combines the `description` and `when_to_use` fields:\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: my-skill\ndescription: What this skill does\nwhen_to_use: Additional context for when Claude should invoke the skill\n---\n```\n\nThe combined text is capped at **1,536 characters** in the skill listing shown to Claude. This truncation serves two purposes:\n\n1. **Reduces context usage**: Skill descriptions stay in context across every turn, so shorter descriptions mean lower token costs\n2. **Prioritizes key information**: You should put the most important use case first in the `description` field\n\n## Best Practices\n\nTo make the most of the 1,536-character budget:\n\n- **Lead with the key use case** in `description`\n- **Keep descriptions concise** — state the purpose clearly without unnecessary elaboration\n- **Use `when_to_use` for additional context** if needed, but recognize it shares the same budget\n- **Write your full detailed instructions in the skill body** (`SKILL.md` content), which loads only when invoked\n\nFor example:\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: commit\ndescription: Stage and commit changes to git\nwhen_to_use: Use when you want to save your work with a descriptive message\n---\n\n1. Stage files with git add\n2. Create a commit with a clear message\n...\n```\n\nThe full skill content only loads when the skill is actually invoked, so verbose instructions don't cost tokens until needed.","durationMs":5736,"url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6a4d4be6-e409-4a36-9191-dd8d5e729ed4","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"83c30d83-83e3-464a-b3bb-0a18b5ea54cb","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
