{"parentUuid":"c07cf731-aa30-4124-8223-eceafd56abed","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad57881598683395e","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf4J4Z2HUBANAudB1PdK6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XZkQfaxyknL3YfpFq35AbP","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"## Claude Code Skill Configuration — Documentation Answers\n\n**1. Does `disable-model-invocation: true` remove skill from model context?**\nYes, fully. Per skills.md: \"The skill's **description is NOT in context** for Claude\" and \"Claude won't see it as an available option.\" Remains in `/skills` menu for manual `/name` invocation only.\n\n**2. What does `skillOverrides` accept?**\nPer skills.md, exactly four values:\n- `\"on\"` — name + description visible to Claude\n- `\"name-only\"` — name only (no description)\n- `\"user-invocable-only\"` — hidden from Claude, marked user-only in `/skills`\n- `\"off\"` — completely hidden, blocks invocation by full name\n\n**3. Is \"user-invocable-only\" equivalent to disable-model-invocation?**\nNo. Key difference: `disable-model-invocation: true` shows skill in `/skills` menu for manual use; `\"user-invocable-only\"` hides it from Claude but appears as user-only in `/skills`.\n\n**4. Character/token budget for skill listings?**\nYes — per skills.md: combined `description` + `when_to_use` capped at **1,536 characters per skill**. When exceeded, text is **truncated at 1,536**, not dropped. Settings `skillListingBudgetFraction` and `skillListingMaxDescChars` provide additional control, but documentation does not specify behavior when overall listing budget is exceeded.\n\n**5. What does `user-invocable: false` do vs. disable-model-invocation?**\nOpposite effect. Per skills.md: description **IS in context**, Claude can auto-invoke it, but **you cannot manually invoke** it with `/skill-name`. Compare to disable-model-invocation, where Claude cannot invoke but you can.\n\n**Not documented:** exact behavior when overall skill listing context budget is exceeded (full skill removal vs. description-only truncation)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":766,"cache_read_input_tokens":38524,"output_tokens":586,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":63},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":766},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":10,"output_tokens":586,"cache_read_input_tokens":38524,"cache_creation_input_tokens":766,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":766,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XZkQfaxyknL3YfpFq35AbP":{"message":"## Claude Code Skill Configuration — Documentation Answers\n\n**1. Does `disable-model-invocation: true` remove skill from model context?**\nYes, fully. Per skills.md: \"The skill's **description is NOT in context** for Claude\" and \"Claude won't see it as an available option.\" Remains in `/skills` menu for manual `/name` invocation only.\n\n**2. What does `skillOverrides` accept?**\nPer skills.md, exactly four values:\n- `\"on\"` — name + description visible to Claude\n- `\"name-only\"` — name only (no description)\n- `\"user-invocable-only\"` — hidden from Claude, marked user-only in `/skills`\n- `\"off\"` — completely hidden, blocks invocation by full name\n\n**3. Is \"user-invocable-only\" equivalent to disable-model-invocation?**\nNo. Key difference: `disable-model-invocation: true` shows skill in `/skills` menu for manual use; `\"user-invocable-only\"` hides it from Claude but appears as user-only in `/skills`.\n\n**4. Character/token budget for skill listings?**\nYes — per skills.md: combined `description` + `when_to_use` capped at **1,536 characters per skill**. When exceeded, text is **truncated at 1,536**, not dropped. Settings `skillListingBudgetFraction` and `skillListingMaxDescChars` provide additional control, but documentation does not specify behavior when overall listing budget is exceeded.\n\n**5. What does `user-invocable: false` do vs. disable-model-invocation?**\nOpposite effect. Per skills.md: description **IS in context**, Claude can auto-invoke it, but **you cannot manually invoke** it with `/skill-name`. Compare to disable-model-invocation, where Claude cannot invoke but you can.\n\n**Not documented:** exact behavior when overall skill listing context budget is exceeded (full skill removal vs. description-only truncation)."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cf4J4YPL4oU5iiLdNks8J","attributionAgent":"claude-code-guide","type":"assistant","uuid":"52955097-f273-41e5-8d5e-30705f6c492a","timestamp":"2026-09-15T00:41:01.824Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"83c30d83-83e3-464a-b3bb-0a18b5ea54cb","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
